"To deal with the `SettingWithCopyWarning` in Pandas, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Check if the warning is coming from a specific function or line of code. In this case, it seems to be coming from the `_decode_stock_quote` function. You can try to suppress this warning by adding the following code before the function:\n\n    ```python\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=SettingWithCopyWarning)\n```\n\n2. If the warning is not coming from a specific function, you can try to suppress it by adding the following code at the top of your script:\n\n    ```python\nimport warnings\nwarnings.simplefilter(action='ignore', category=SettingWithCopyWarning)\n```\n\n3. If you really need to use the line of code that is causing the warning, you can try to use the `.loc` accessor instead of `.iloc` to avoid creating a copy of the DataFrame:\n\n    ```python\nquote_df = quote_df.loc[:, [0, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5, 8, 9, 30, 31]]\n```\n\n4. Alternatively, you can try to avoid using the line of code that is causing the warning by reorganizing your data or using a different approach.\n\n5. If none of the above steps work, you can try to update the `SettingWithCopyWarning` to a more general warning:\n\n    ```python\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=FutureWarning)\n```"
"None\n# Creating an empty DataFrame and adding rows one by one\n#========================================================\n\nYou can use the `loc` attribute of the DataFrame to add new rows one by one. This is a more efficient and flexible way than using the `set_value` method.\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Create an empty DataFrame\ndf = pd.DataFrame(columns=('lib', 'qty1', 'qty2'))\n\n# Add a new row at the end and fill a single field with 10.0\ndf.loc[len(df)] = {'qty1': 10.0}  # Add a new row at the end\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can use the `concat` function to add multiple rows at once.\n\n```python\n# Add a new row at the end and fill a single field with 10.0\ndf = pd.concat([df, pd.DataFrame({'qty1': [10.0]})], ignore_index=True)\n```"
