"```python\ndef traverse_reverse(collection):\n    \"\"\"Traverse a list in reverse order, starting from the end and ending at the beginning.\"\"\"\n    for index, value in enumerate(reversed(collection)):\n        yield value, index\n\n# Example usage:\nmy_list = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nfor value, index in traverse_reverse(my_list):\n    print(f\"Value: {value}, Index: {index}\")\n```\n\nThis code defines a generator function `traverse_reverse` that takes a list as input and yields the value and its index in reverse order. The `enumerate` function is used to get both the index and value of each element in the list. The `reversed` function is used to reverse the order of the list. The example usage demonstrates how to use the generator to traverse the list and access the loop index."
