"None\nTo enable mod_rewrite for Apache 2.2, you need to load the rewrite module and define your rewrite rules. The issue you're facing might be due to a configuration issue or a firewall blocking the mod_rewrite module.\n\nHere's a simple example of how to enable mod_rewrite:\n\n```bash\n# Load the rewrite module\nLoadModule rewrite_module modules/mod_rewrite.so\n\n# Define a basic rewrite rule\nRewriteRule ^(.*)$ http://example.com/$1 [L]\n```\n\nThis rule will redirect any URL that starts with a dot (.) to a URL that starts with http://example.com/. The [L] at the end means it's the last rule defined in the document, so it will block any further requests.\n\nMake sure to place this code in the .htaccess file of your Apache server (usually located at /etc/apache2/apache2.conf or /etc/apache2/apache2.conf.d/*.conf). \n\nIf you're still having issues, try checking the Apache error log for any error messages that might indicate what's going wrong."
