"None\nThe word 'logits' in TensorFlow refers to the output of the last layer of a neural network, which is a mathematical function that maps the input data to a probability distribution over the possible classes or labels. This is in contrast to 'scores', which are the output of the neural network after passing through the final layer, but not necessarily a probability distribution."
"None\nimport tensorflow as tf\n\ndef max_pool(x, k, strides=None, padding='SAME'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Apply max pooling to the input tensor x.\n\n    Args:\n    x (tensor): The input tensor.\n    k (int): The size of the pooling window.\n    strides (tuple, optional): The stride of the pooling operation. Defaults to None.\n    padding (str, optional): The padding mode. Defaults to 'SAME'.\n\n    Returns:\n    tensor: The output tensor after max pooling.\n    \"\"\"\n    if strides is None:\n        strides = (1, 1)\n    output = tf.nn.max_pool(x, k, strides, padding)\n    return output"
