"```python\nimport tensorflow as tf\n\ndef tf_variable_scope(name_or_scope, reuse=None, initializer=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a context for variable scope.\n    \n    Args:\n    - name_or_scope (str): The name of the variable scope or the variable itself.\n    - reuse (bool, optional): Whether to reuse the variable scope. Defaults to None.\n    - initializer (tf.Variable_initializer, optional): The initial value of the variable. Defaults to None.\n    \n    Returns:\n    - tf.VariableScope: A context for variable scope.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a new variable scope with the given name or variable\n    with tf.variable_scope(name_or_scope, reuse=reuse, initializer=initializer):\n        # Return the variable scope\n        return tf.VariableScope(name_or_scope)\n```\n\nYou can use this function to create a variable scope with a specific name, or reuse an existing variable scope. The `initializer` parameter allows you to specify an initial value for the variable."
