"```python\nimport clr\n\n# Add the COM assembly containing the resources\nclr.AddReference('System.Windows.Forms', 'System.Windows.Forms')\n\n# Load the resources from the assembly\nresources = clr.AddReference('System.Windows.Forms', 'System.Windows.Forms')\nresources.Load('ResourceDictionary')\n\n# Create a ResourceDictionary object\nresource_dict = resources.GetManifestResourceObject('ResourceDictionary')\n\n# Load the resource dictionaries from the assembly\nmenu_template = resource_dict.GetManifestResourceObject('MenuTemplate.xaml')\nbutton_template = resource_dict.GetManifestResourceObject('ButtonTemplate.xaml')\n\n# Merge the resource dictionaries into a single dictionary\nmerged_dict = resource_dict.MergedDictionaries()\nmerged_dict['MenuTemplate'] = menu_template\nmerged_dict['ButtonTemplate'] = button_template\n```"
"None\n\nTo make a WPF TextBlock selectable, you can use the `TextBlock`'s `IsEditable` property. By default, this property is set to `False`, which means the text is not selectable. However, you can set it to `True` to enable text selection. \n\nHere is an example:\n\n```python\nfrom wpf import TextBlock\n\ntext_block = TextBlock()\ntext_block.IsEditable = True\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can use a `RichTextBlock` which is designed specifically for displaying rich text and has built-in support for selecting and editing text. \n\n```python\nfrom wpf import RichTextBlock\n\ntext_block = RichTextBlock()\ntext_block.IsEditable = True\n```"
"def properties_order(xaml_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the properties order from XAML string.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    xaml_string (str): The XAML string containing the properties order.\n    \n    Returns:\n    dict: A dictionary containing the properties order as keys and their corresponding values.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Initialize an empty dictionary to store the properties order\n    order = {}\n    \n    # Split the XAML string into lines\n    lines = xaml_string.split('\\n')\n    \n    # Iterate over each line in the XAML string\n    for line in lines:\n        # Check if the line contains a property with a value\n        if 'From' in line:\n            # Extract the property name and value\n            prop_name, value = line.split('From=\"')\n            value = value.strip('\"')\n            \n            # Add the property to the dictionary\n            order[prop_name] = value\n    \n    # Return the dictionary containing the properties order\n    return order\n\nxaml_string = \"\"\"\nStoryboard.TargetProperty=\"Margin\" From=\"1,2,3,4\" To=\"0,0,0,0\"\n\"\"\"\norder = properties_order(xaml_string)\nprint(order)\nprint(order.keys())  # Output: ['From', 'To']\nprint(order[1])   # Output: 3\nprint(order[2])   # Output: 0\nprint(order[3])   # Output: 0\nprint(order[4])   # Output: 4"
"```csharp\nusing System.ComponentModel;\nusing System.ComponentModel.Design;\nusing System.Net.Http;\nusing System.Net.Http.Headers;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\n\npublic class FacebookFriendsList\n{\n    public async Task<string> ExecuteAsync()\n    {\n        using (var client = new HttpClient())\n        {\n            var response = await client.GetAsync(\"https://graph.facebook.com/v13.0/me/friends?fields=id,name&access_token=YOUR_APP_ACCESS_TOKEN\");\n\n            if (response.IsSuccessStatusCode)\n            {\n                var data = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();\n                return data;\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                throw new Exception(\"Failed to retrieve friends\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\npublic class BackgroundWorker : BackgroundWorker\n{\n    public async Task Main(string[] args)\n    {\n        // Define the worker's work\n        DoWork += (sender, e) =>\n        {\n            var ffl = new FacebookFriendsList();\n            Console.WriteLine(e.Argument);\n            // Perform time-consuming task...\n            await Task.Delay(2000);\n        };\n\n        // Start the worker\n        RunWorkerAsync(\"Message to worker\", null, null, null);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nYou can replace `YOUR_APP_ACCESS_TOKEN` with your actual Facebook app access token."
"```python\nfrom WindowsFormsApp1 import Application, Window\n\ndef hide_close_button():\n    # Create a new application\n    app = Application()\n\n    # Create a new window\n    window = Window()\n\n    # Set the window style to be a modal window with a normal title bar\n    window.WindowStyle = WindowStyle.Modal | WindowStyle.Maximized\n\n    # Set the window state to be non-modal\n    window.WindowState = WindowState.Minimized\n\n    # Set the window size to be 200x100\n    window.Size = (200, 100)\n\n    # Set the window resize mode to be None (auto)\n    window.ResizeMode = ResizeMode.None\n\n    # Show the window\n    window.Show()\n\n    # Wait for 5 seconds\n    import time\n    time.sleep(5)\n\n    # Close the window\n    window.Close()\n\n# Call the function\nhide_close_button()\n```"
