"To fix this issue, you can create a custom Git hook in your Git repository. A hook is a script that runs automatically after a certain event, such as a commit or push. You can create a hook that updates the email address in your local Git repository and then runs a script that checks the email address against Jenkins' email list.\n\nHere's an example of how you can create a custom Git hook:\n\n```bash\n# .git/hooks/post-commit\n#!/bin/bash\n\n# Get the email address from the commit message\nCOMMIT_MESSAGE=$(git show -s --format=%s HEAD)\n\n# Get the email list from Jenkins\nEMAIL_LIST=$(cat <<EOF\n<list of email addresses>\nabc.example@example.com\ndef.example@example.com\nEOF\n)\n\n# Check if the email address in the commit message matches any in the list\nif [[ $COMMIT_MESSAGE =~ @abc.example ]]; then\n  # If it matches, update the email address in your local Git repository\n  git config --global user.name \"New Email Name\"\n  git config --global user.email \"newemail@example.com\"\n  echo \"Email address updated successfully.\"\nelse\n  echo \"Email address does not match any in the list.\"\nfi\n```\n\nTo make this script run after every commit, you can add it to the `.git/hooks/post-commit` file.\n\nAlternatively, you can also use a Git hook to update the email address in your local Git repository when a push occurs:\n\n```bash\n# .git/hooks/post-receive\n#!/bin/bash\n\n# Get the email address from the push message\nREMOTE_USER=$(git show -s --format=%s HEAD)\n\n# Get the email list from Jenkins\nEMAIL_LIST=$(cat <<EOF\n<list of email addresses>\nabc.example@example.com\ndef.example@example.com\nEOF\n)\n\n# Check if the email address in the push message matches any in the list\nif [[ $REMOTE_USER =~ @abc.example ]]; then\n  # If it matches, update the email address in your local Git repository\n  git config --global user.name \"New Email Name\"\n  git config --global user.email \"newemail@example.com\"\n  echo \"Email address updated successfully.\"\nelse\n  echo \"Email address does not match any in the list.\"\nfi\n```\n\nTo make this script run after every push, you can add it to the `.git/hooks/post-receive` file.\n\nOnce you've created and saved these scripts, you can test them by committing a change and pushing it to your Git repository. The email address should be updated correctly."
